 Jensen Ackles makes his much-anticipated return as Russell Shaw in the latest episode of Tracker . This time, the brothers aren't rehashing old resentments; they're solving a case together. Russell's former military colleague, Grant Valko, is in trouble after his wife and daughter are kidnapped by people trying to cover up an incident Grant witnessed during a mission.
 Russell lets Colter know that he will get a call from Grant. When Colter discovers that Russell is back in town and is following a related lead, the brothers join forces to find the missing family and the operation behind it.
 The case falls under familiar Tracker territory, so the real fun comes from seeing Colter approach the job with someone who can match his experience.
 He's spent most of the series working alone in the field, relying on Reenie and Randy for information. He rarely has another investigator by his side. Ackles changes that dynamic and brings his own military background and instincts. The two work the problem out from different angles.
 Thanks to Colter and Russell's combined efforts, Tracker Season 4, Episode 5, moves quickly. The added support also makes the danger feel closer and more immediate. Of course, it's a pleasure to see the Shaw brothers interact again. They have an easygoing vibe, and their exchanges bring some much-needed humor to the episode. After the case, Colter asks Russell if this is the part where he disappears again, poking fun at his brother's explanation that surfing is the reason why he was away.
 While it's a lighthearted scene, there's history behind it. Russell has a habit of leaving , and Colter clearly hasn't forgotten that. The show perfectly examines their complicated relationship without letting it overshadow the action.
